 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: Proportional to the area of the triangle's bounding box projected onto the dominant axis plane, multiplied by the depth range in the dominant axis direction. For sparse grids, this is significantly faster than full 3D clipping for large triangles.
-- **Memory Complexity**: Proportional to the number of voxels intersected by the triangle. Stored in a sparse array indexed by Morton codes [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths**: Optimizes for sparse storage by avoiding unnecessary voxel checks in empty columns. Efficient for large triangles spanning many voxels.
-- **Limitations**: Requires careful handling of edge cases (division by zero, clamping errors). Multi-pass mode requires pre-computation and buffer management.
-- **When to Use**: When voxelizing large triangles into a sparse voxel DAG and performance is critical.
-- **When Not to Use**: For very small triangles or dense grids where the overhead of dominant axis calculation outweighs the benefits.
